但你听着。

277
00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.460
His name is Michael Scott.
他的名字叫迈克尔·斯科特。

278
00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.260
No.
不是。

279
00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.060
Lieberthal.
利伯塔尔。

280
00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:21.860
No.
不是。

281
00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.200
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特。

282
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.420
I even looked that up.
我甚至查过那个。

283
00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:25.960
I didn't come across the middle name.
我没看到中间名是那个。

284
00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:26.300
Yeah.
是啊。

285
00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:27.340
Wow.
哇。

286
00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:28.600
Another Michael Scott.
又一个迈克尔·斯科特。

287
00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:29.460
All right.
好吧。

288
00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.360
Here's my last Michael Scott for you.
这是我为你准备的最后一个迈克尔·斯科特。

289
00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:31.800
Okay.
好的。

290
00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:36.980
There's a famous Irish writer named Michael Scott.
有一位著名的爱尔兰作家叫迈克尔·斯科特。

291
00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.300
And he writes science fiction.
他写科幻小说。

292
00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.460
Angela, you'd like him.
安吉拉，你会喜欢他的。

293
00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:41.060
Fantasy.
奇幻小说。

294
00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:41.520
Horror.
恐怖小说。

295
00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.700
He's written over 100 books.
他写了超过100本书。

296
00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:49.720
And he's maybe most famous for this series called The Secrets of the Immortal Nicholas Flannel.
他最出名的可能是一个叫《不朽的尼古拉斯·弗拉梅尔的秘密》的系列。

297
00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:54.540
But in all my reading about him, I am pretty sure his life has been made completely miserable
但在我读过的所有关于他的资料中，我很确定他的生活已经被迈克尔·斯科特这个角色

298
00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.720
by the character of Michael Scott.
搞得一团糟了。

299
00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:58.560
Well, yeah.
嗯，确实。

300
00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:05.320
Because he's like this accomplished novelist who was very famous.
因为他是一位非常有名的成就卓著的小说家。

301
00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:11.600
And then when this man was like around 60 or 65 years old, a television show called
等到这位先生大约60或65岁的时候，一部名为

302
00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:14.520
The Office came around and turned his name into a joke.
《办公室》的电视剧出现了，并把他的名字变成了一个笑话。

303
00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:17.860
So we're very sorry, Irish writer Michael Scott.
所以我们非常抱歉，爱尔兰作家迈克尔·斯科特。

304
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.980
But I hope now people go check out your books.
但我希望现在人们会去看看你的书。

305
00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:20.400
Yeah.
是啊。

306
00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:21.400
Well, there we go.
好吧，就是这样。

307
00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:22.620
I needed to give him a plug.
我得帮他宣传一下。

308
00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:26.100
I mean, they were at the top of the New York Times bestseller list and all.
我的意思是，它们当时可是登上了《纽约时报》畅销书排行榜榜首的。

309
00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.480
Oh, I want to check them out.
哦，我想去看看。

310
00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:27.880
Yeah, it's good stuff.
是啊，是很棒的作品。

311
00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:28.620
I probably love them.
我大概会很喜欢。

312
00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:28.980
Yeah.
是啊。

313
00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:30.220
All right.
好吧。

314
00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.140
Well, that's it.
好了，就这样。

315
00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:32.940
That's all I got for my fast facts.
这就是我准备的所有快讯了。

316
00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.660
Those were really good fast facts.
那些快讯真的很棒。

317
00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:36.840
I think we had a good time in that section.
我觉得我们在那个环节玩得很开心。

318
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:37.460
Thank you.
谢谢。

319
00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:38.560
Well, we'll take a break.
好了，我们休息一下。

320
00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:51.580
To this episode, Jenna, I have something right away at 43 seconds.
对于这一集，珍娜，我在43秒处立刻就发现了一些东西。

321
00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.200
Dwight starts his interrogation.
德怀特开始了审讯。

322
00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:54.740
Yeah.
是啊。

323
00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.060
First one up is Kevin.
第一个是凯文。

324
00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.300
And he says, here are the symptoms of marijuana use.
他说，这是吸食大麻的症状。

325
00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.880
Tell me if any of these remind you of someone.
告诉我这些症状里有没有让你想起谁的。

326
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.120
Number one, slow moving.
第一，行动迟缓。

327
00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.840
Two, inattentive.
第二，注意力不集中。

328
00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.120
Three, dull.
第三，迟钝。

329
00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.640
Four, constantly snacking.
第四，不停地吃零食。

330
00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:13.960
Five, shows a lack of motivation.
第五，表现出缺乏动力。

331
00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.780
Kevin responds, hey.
凯文回应说，嘿。

332
00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:17.400
Yeah.
是啊。

333
00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:22.800
Okay, there is a blooper that I had never seen.
好的，有一个我从未见过的NG片段。

334
00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:25.340
I've watched a lot of these bloopers now, right?
我现在看了很多这样的NG片段，对吧？

335
00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:25.660
Yeah.
是啊。

336
00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:29.120
And there's sort of different compilations of them on YouTube.
YouTube上还有各种不同的合集。

337
00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:35.200
I don't know how I missed it, but there is a blooper where Kevin is talking to you at front reception.
我不知道我是怎么错过的，但有一个NG片段是凯文在前台跟你说话。

338
00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:37.820
And he goes, he said I was dull.
他说，他说我很迟钝。

339
00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.680
And you can't get through it.
你根本演不下去。

340
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:40.800
You keep laughing.
你一直在笑。

341
00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:43.560
I could not do Kevin's scenes.
我没法演凯文的戏份。

342
00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:48.340
Brian made me laugh so hard all the time.
布莱恩总是把我逗得大笑不止。

343
00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.040
You had no lines.
你当时没有台词。

344
00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:50.400
No.
没有。

345
00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.640
All he said was, he said I was dull.
他只说了句，他说我很迟钝。

346
00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.820
And you couldn't even look at him.
你甚至都没法看他一眼。

347
00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:55.760
I remember that.
我记得那个。

348
00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.120
I remember shooting that.
我记得拍摄那场戏的时候。

349
00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:57.600
Yeah.
是啊。

350
00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.320
Because I don't think we got it.
因为我觉得我们当时没拍成。

351
00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.360
I think the reason it's not in the episode is we never got a take of it.
我觉得这一段没出现在剧集里是因为我们从来没拍到过。

352
00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:03.240
I couldn't do it.
我做不到。

353
00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:04.680
I mean, I don't doubt it.
我是说，我不怀疑这一点。

354
00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.060
That happens sometimes.
这种情况时有发生。

355
00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.340
Sometimes they were like, you know what?
有时候他们会说，你知道吗？

356
00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:07.980
It's a wash.
算了。

357
00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:08.500
Never mind.
没关系。

358
00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:09.200
Just leave it alone.
别管它了。

359
00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:09.900
We have enough.
我们有足够的素材了。

360
00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:10.460
We have enough.
我们有足够的素材了。

361
00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:15.800
And then Dwight in a talking head right after says, I like the people I work with, with the exception of four.
然后德怀特紧接着在采访中说，我喜欢和我一起工作的人，除了四个人之外。

362
00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:16.960
Four people.
四个人。

363
00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.260
Who are those four people?
那四个人是谁？

364
00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:20.020
We got a lot of mail about that.
我们收到了很多关于这个问题的来信。

365
00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:20.540
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

366
00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:21.820
Well, what did you find?
那么，你们发现了什么？

367
00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:23.700
I don't know.
我不知道。

368
00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:31.000
People wanted us to name the four people that we think are the four people, with the exception of four people.
大家想让我们列出那四个人，就是我们认为他不喜欢的那四个人。

369
00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:31.760
Who do you think?
你觉得是谁？

370
00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.260
Who do I think he does like or doesn't like?
你是指我猜他喜欢谁，还是不喜欢谁？

371
00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:37.060
No, he says he likes everyone with the exception of four.
不，他说他喜欢所有人，除了四个人。

372
00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:37.400
With the exception of four people.
除了四个人之外。

373
00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.940
Who do I think he doesn't like?
你觉得他不喜欢谁？

374
00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.520
I think he doesn't like Jim.
我觉得他不喜欢吉姆。

375
00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:45.080
Oh, Jim is number one on the list for me.
哦，在我看来吉姆绝对是名单上的第一名。

376
00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.360
I think he doesn't like Creed?
我觉得他不喜欢克里德？

377
00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:49.520
Creed?
克里德？

378
00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:56.320
I would say Toby just because Michael hates Toby and Dwight loves Michael.
我会说是托比，因为迈克尔讨厌托比，而德怀特崇拜迈克尔。

379
00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.080
He might.
他可能确实不喜欢。

380
00:15:57.320 --> 00:15:58.480
Well, he likes Pam.
嗯，他喜欢帕姆。

381
00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.420
We know that.
我们都知道这一点。

382
00:15:59.520 --> 00:15:59.700
Yeah.
是啊。

383
00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.320
He's got a soft spot for Pam.
他对帕姆情有独钟。

384
00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.040
I think he thinks Pam's decent.
我觉得他认为帕姆还不错。

385
00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:04.700
Maybe Ryan and Kelly.
也许是瑞安和凯莉。

386
00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:08.980
Maybe Ryan the temp because he's competition to him.
也许是临时工瑞安，因为他是他的竞争对手。

387
00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:14.420
And then maybe because he's competitive, maybe one of the other sales reps.
还有因为他好胜，也许是其他销售代表中的一个。

388
00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:15.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

389
00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:15.500
Yeah.
是啊。

390
00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:16.940
All right.
好吧。

391
00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:17.760
There you go.
就是这样。

392
00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:18.180
We don't know, though.
不过我们确实不知道。

393
00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:18.740
We don't know.
我们不知道。

394
00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:19.920
We don't know who the four people are.
我们不知道那四个人到底是谁。

395
00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.140
They were never written down.
剧本里从来没写过。

396
00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.340
That's one of those fun little things that we just give you to think about.
这是我们留给你们思考的有趣小细节之一。

397
00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:25.820
Yeah.
是啊。

398
00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:26.400
The writers.
编剧们。

399
00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.540
You tell us who you think.
你们告诉我们你们觉得是谁。

400
00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:27.880
Yeah.
是啊。

401
00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:32.840
So now we're in the kitchen, and Jim does an impression of Stanley.
现在我们在厨房里，吉姆在模仿斯坦利。

402
00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:33.620
Yes.
没错。

403
00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.300
Followed by a Pam talking head doing an impression of Phyllis.
接着是帕姆的采访镜头，她在模仿菲利斯。

404
00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:37.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

405
00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:42.780
Tina Kekalik, Michaela Maroney, and Katie Coles all ask this question.
蒂娜·凯卡利克、米凯拉·马罗尼和凯蒂·科尔斯都问了这个问题。

406
00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:49.080
Did the writers know that John could do impressions of Stanley ahead of time, or did they just write
编剧们是提前知道约翰会模仿斯坦利，还是只是写了剧本

407
00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.460
it and hope he could do it?
然后希望他能演出来？

408
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:56.980
Guys, John Krasinski's impressions were known and legendary.
伙计们，约翰·卡拉辛斯基的模仿功力可是出了名的，堪称传奇。

409
00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:00.860
Guys, we were like 20 episodes in by now, and we were all hanging out a lot.
伙计们，当时我们已经拍了大概20集了，大家经常待在一起。

410
00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:05.040
And in between scenes or when we were killing time and goofing off, John would do these
在拍摄间隙，或者我们打发时间胡闹的时候，约翰就会做这些

411
00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.480
impressions, and we loved them.
模仿表演，我们都特别喜欢。

412
00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:11.900
John could be one of those Saturday Night Live people who does impressions of people.
约翰完全可以成为那种在《周六夜现场》里模仿各路明星的人。

413
00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.720
Like, he is an amazing mimic.
他简直是个模仿天才。

414
00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:15.020
Yes.
没错。

415
00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:15.840
The writers knew.
编剧们是知道的。

416
00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:16.800
The writers knew.
编剧们是知道的。

417
00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:18.220
It's on the DVD commentary, too.
DVD评论音轨里也提到了。

418
00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.860
They talk about it, about how great he is with impressions.
他们谈到了这一点，说他模仿得有多棒。

419
00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:22.680
I am horrible at impressions.
我模仿得特别烂。

420
00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:26.420
You made me laugh really hard with your Phyllis impression.
你模仿菲利斯的时候把我逗得大笑不止。

421
00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:31.700
And then here's something I thought was so clever, is your talking head is by the kitchen
还有一点我觉得特别巧妙，就是你的采访镜头是在厨房

422
00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:36.220
door that has a window, and over your shoulder, you can see Phyllis and Jim.
门边，那里有个窗户，透过窗户你可以看到菲利斯和吉姆。

423
00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:36.560
Yeah.
是啊。

424
00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:41.100
Which is, Pam has some interesting talking heads location-wise in this episode.
这一集里帕姆的采访地点选得挺有意思的。

425
00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:41.820
I agree.
我同意。

426
00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:42.340
Yeah.
没错。

427
00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.620
That was planned.
那是刻意安排的。

428
00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:44.180
Yeah.
是啊。

429
00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:45.840
They wanted you to see them in the background.
他们想让你在背景里看到他们。

430
00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:46.560
Yeah.
没错。

431
00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:47.000
Yeah.
是啊。

432
00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.160
Instead of in the chair.
而不是坐在椅子上。

433
00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:48.560
Yeah.
没错。

434
00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.460
Where I normally sit.
也就是我平时坐的地方。

435
00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:54.700
But if you watch the deleted scenes, you can see John doing impressions of more people.
但如果你看删减片段，还能看到约翰模仿更多人。

436
00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.600
So if you want more, you can have more.
所以如果你想看更多，还有更多内容。

437
00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.700
And they're great.
而且都很棒。

438
00:17:58.860 --> 00:17:59.260
They're great.
真的很棒。

439
00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.940
He does several other, like, members of the office.
他还模仿了办公室里的其他几个人。

440
00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:05.300
At two minutes, 19 seconds, we're in the conference room.
在两分十九秒时，我们在会议室里。

441
00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.940
Dwight is interrogating Kelly.
德怀特正在审问凯莉。

442
00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.280
I swear it looks like rain is going to break at any moment.
我发誓看起来随时都要下雨了。

443
00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:13.460
Well, they could not get through this scene.
嗯，他们当时拍这场戏一直笑场。

444
00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.000
I remember this, like, so vividly.
我记得特别清楚。

445
00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.780
Mindy was, like, on the floor.
敏迪当时整个人都笑瘫在地上了。

446
00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.140
She had disintegrated.
她简直笑到崩溃。

447
00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:25.420
And if you watch the scene, when he goes, your ass is on the line.
如果你看这场戏，当他说出“你的屁股就在线上”时，

448
00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:26.840
My ass is on the line.
“我的屁股就在线上。”

449
00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.660
It barely cuts to Mindy.
镜头几乎没怎么给到敏迪。

450
00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:29.600
It's so quick.
切得太快了。

451
00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:31.420
Because she couldn't get through it.
因为她没法演完那段戏。

452
00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:35.340
That might be the only reaction they have where she isn't just giggling.
那可能是她唯一一次没有在那儿傻笑的反应了。

453
00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:35.740
Yeah.
是啊。

454
00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:44.760
I feel like rain is about to lose it right after he says, this is not Kelly Kapoor's story hour.
我觉得雷恩在说完“这不是凯莉·卡普尔的故事时间”之后，差点就要笑场了。

455
00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:45.220
Yeah.
没错。

456
00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:48.140
Like, he has to, like, purse his lips a little bit.
你看，他不得不稍微抿了抿嘴。

457
00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:48.500
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

458
00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:51.220
I want you to notice something in this scene, by the way.
顺便说一下，我想让你们注意这个场景里的一个细节。

459
00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:51.700
What?
什么？

460
00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:53.640
Mindy's hair is up.
敏迪把头发盘起来了。

461
00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:54.080
Yeah.
是啊。

462
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:56.460
In kind of a twisty thing.
盘成了一种扭转的造型。

463
00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:57.620
It's a stylish twiSt.
那是一种时髦的盘发。

464
00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:57.980
Yeah.
没错。

465
00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:59.580
Do you know why her hair is up?
你们知道她为什么要盘头发吗？

466
00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:01.920
Is it because she got extensions?
是因为她接了长发吗？

467
00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:03.180
For Casino Night.
为了拍“赌场之夜”。

468
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:06.120
And we shot Casino Night before this.
我们是在拍这一集之前拍的“赌场之夜”。

469
00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:10.880
She's also wearing, like, a colorful shirt, but then, like, this pink sweater shawl thing.
她还穿了一件花哨的衬衫，外面套了件粉色的毛衣披肩之类的东西。

470
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.600
A very fuzzy shawl.
一件毛茸茸的披肩。

471
00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.000
Half sweater thing.
半件毛衣那样的东西。

472
00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:15.440
Like an Angora sweater thing.
像安哥拉兔毛毛衣之类的。

473
00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:15.720
Yeah.
对。

474
00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:16.480
Yeah.
没错。

475
00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.380
But anyway, that's why her hair is up.
总之，这就是她盘头发的原因。

476
00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:18.660
Well.
好吧。

477
00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.460
Because it's longer.
因为头发变长了。

478
00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:20.300
Continuity.
为了连戏。

479
00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:21.640
That's real good.
这解释得真好。

480
00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.560
So next up, Dwight goes over to Ryan.
接下来，德怀特走向雷恩。

481
00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:26.720
He says, I want to search your car.
他说，我要搜查你的车。

482
00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.000
Give me your keys.
把钥匙给我。

483
00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.140
I want to search your car.
我要搜查你的车。

484
